    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and adapt to a student’s pace. They can break down tough topics into relatable examples, like using real-life scenarios to teach equations. This helps reduce anxiety and makes learning feel less like memorization and more like exploration—especially for students who don’t naturally feel confident in math."
